WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.420
On a dry, windy sand dune, marram
grass rolls its leaves up tight.

2
00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:08.660
A cactus has given up
proper leaves altogether.

3
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:11.620
It has spines, and a fat green stem.

4
00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:16.860
But first, any plant must get water
in, through its fine root hairs.

5
00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:20.420
So how does water get
from the soil into a root,

6
00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:23.160
and how do desert plants keep hold of it?

7
00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.740
In this mission, you'll peel back a root,

8
00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.840
layer by layer, from the hairs inwards.

9
00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:33.680
Then you'll open a toolbox of tricks
that plants use in dry places.

10
00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:37.430
Your mission: find out how
water gets into a root,

11
00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.810
and how desert plants keep hold of it.
